[38;5;252m[1m## The mismatch: [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust binary exited 0 where the C binary died from signal 13 (shell status 141). The Rust standard library installs [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m runs, so a write to a closed stdout came back as an ignored [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m error and the program ran to completion. C has no such handler — the write is fatal.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10m$ python3 -c "print('6\n'*200)" > /tmp/big.txt
$ ( c_src/build/driver < /tmp/big.txt; echo rc=$? >&2 ) 2>&1 | head -c 100 >/dev/null
rc=141
$ ( translation/.../driver < /tmp/big.txt; echo rc=$? >&2 ) 2>&1 | head -c 100 >/dev/null
rc=0          # before the fix
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
stdout was byte-identical in this case — only the exit status differed, so a stdout-only comparison would have passed. Fixed by [38;5;10mrestore_default_sigpipe()[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m, which resets the disposition to [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m.[0m[0m
